  "verbalization": "Licorice glycoside D2 is implicated in the regulation of DNA polymerase eta through a multi-step mechanism involving the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex. This complex is targeted by multiple compounds, including Cassiaoccidentalin B, 2-Oxaisodauc-5-En-12-Al, and Namogenin C, all of which direct their activity toward DNA polymerase eta. The presence of a final score of 0.5217 across these paths suggests a consistent and plausible biological relationship, though the exact nature of the interaction remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a pathway where Licorice glycoside D2 acts as a modulator of the EZH2/SUZ12/EED complex, which in turn influences DNA polymerase eta activity. The integration of these findings implies that Licorice glycoside D2 may exert its effects by targeting the epigenetic machinery that regulates DNA polymerase eta, potentially through the inhibition of its enzymatic activity or by altering its expression. The mechanism is supported by the shared target of multiple compounds, indicating a possible role in the regulation of DNA polymerase eta in cellular processes.",
